  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nRidging building today through Thursday will gradually dry\nthings out and allow for a warming trend as we enter October. \nProbabilities of exceeding 80F by Thursday are in the 60-90% \nrange for all areas except the I-80 corridor and the ridges. \nDepending on shower activity and cloud cover Friday there is \nstill a shot at 80F though the probabilities are lower.\n\nThe trend has continued to be drier for Thursday and it now\nappears that precipitation likely waits until Friday and on into\nthe weekend. There are more scenarios now that keep a Thursday\nshort wave well north in Ontario and the ridge keeps hold on\narea. A more significant trough is shown to dig across the Great\nLakes and bring a front with showers over the weekend.  \n\nProbabilities of exceeding 0.25\" of rain increase to 40-60%\nSaturday and 45-70% on Sunday with highest probabilities in West\nVirginia and lowest probabilities along the I-80 corridor. The\nwet weather over the weekend will also result in cooling with\nhighs mainly in the 60s.",
